{
  "name": "Backdated MTM valuations for counterparty audit requests",
  "today": "Counterparties' auditors ask the Confirmations group (Larry Joe Hunter, Ellen Wallumrod) for mark-to-market values of the counterparty's deals as of a past date. Confirmations has no system that values deals, so they email five or six desk heads. Each desk head forwards the request to an analyst, who runs a mini-book as of that date, exports it to Excel, blacks out sensitive columns (Delta/Vol), and sends totals back up through the desk head.",
  "change": "Give Confirmations a read-only counterparty MTM report with back-dated curves so they answer auditor requests themselves instead of emailing every desk.",
  "explanation": "Build the EnTelligence view Hunter describes (back-dated curves, no Delta/Vol), or a standard query of official valuations by counterparty short name and as-of date that leaves out Delta/Vol. Confirmations would use it. They enter the counterparty and date, check the totals and send them to the auditor. Desks are contacted only for exceptions. Desk heads no longer forward requests, analysts no longer run backdated mini-books, and nobody blacks out columns by hand.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/240.eml",
      "quote": "Please forward to Ellen Wallumrod the MTM valuation(mini-book) for all \nCoEnergy Trading Company deals as of Dec 31, 2000."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/214.eml",
      "quote": "Can you provide MTM values as of Dec 29, 2000, for the short name of CROSS \nTIMBERS."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Two more counterparties need MTM values for Dec. 29, 2000."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/136.eml",
      "quote": "The following are the totals for Tudor BVI and Ospraie.  The total MTM value \nfor the West Desk are as follows."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "We do not have access to \nany system that values these deals, but are looking to get the on-line \n\"EnTelligence\" built so that it carries back-dated curves that will allow us \nto complete these requests without taking up a Risk person's time and without \nhaving to black out information (Delta/Vol) that is included in a mini-book.",
      "note": "Confirmations cannot value deals, so every request takes a Risk analyst's time and needs columns blacked out by hand. The proposed report removes both."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "Until we can get EnTelligence built to our specifications, \nwe'll need to continue to go to the different desks to provide Mark-to-Market \nvaluations for a Counterparty's portfolio.",
      "note": "Each request goes out to every desk."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the total MTM value for that date within your region.",
      "note": "Each desk has to produce its own total, which Confirmations then adds up."
    }
  ],
  "stalls": [],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 3,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
    "quote": "we recieve several \nper week"
  },
  "minutes": 55
}

{
  "name": "Backdated MTM valuations for counterparty audit requests",
  "change": "Give Confirmations a read-only counterparty MTM report with back-dated curves so they answer auditor requests themselves instead of emailing every desk.",
  "reason": "This work is already saved as 'Back-dated MTM valuations for counterparty audit requests', which cites the same five messages (giron-d/sent/136, 137, 214, 240, 241) and proposes the same report.",
  "research": null
}

{
  "name": "Credit Report wrong-entity TAGG rebooks and desk forwarding",
  "change": "Block known wrong-entity counterparties at TAGG deal entry with a credit-kept 'use instead' mapping, and route each Credit Report row to the owning book administrator.",
  "reason": "The 65 minutes a day rests on a 'fixed mapping' that the mail contradicts (the Aquila/Utilicorp rebook runs in opposite directions, the Louis Dreyfus target changes, and AEP Energy Services, Inc. is rebooked to itself), on a repeat rate of half when the cited reports show about a third, and on six desk heads forwarding every day when only Giron's forwards, often sent days late in batches, appear in the mail.",
  "research": "Count rebook lines across all 71 reports in giron-d/sent and keep only counterparty pairs that always have the same target. Find mail from book administrators or Confirmations, such as Julie Brewer's chase in 124.eml, that shows who actually rebooks and how long it takes. Check whether desk heads other than Giron forward the report at all, given that the book administrators are already on its distribution list."
}

{
  "name": "Searching all books and flipping ECC third-party deals to FT-US/CAND-ERMS before NYMEX invoicing",
  "change": "Auto-book ECC-mastered counterparty deals to FT-US/CAND-ERMS and replace the all-books request waves with a nightly exception report.",
  "reason": "The same work and change are already saved as item 3 in decisions.md, 'Monthly hunt for Enron Canada (ECC) deals in Houston books before NYMEX invoicing', which cites the same messages (giron-d/sent/108, 195, 270, 292, 360, 539, 550).",
  "research": null
}

{
  "name": "Hourly phone check-out of service-customer generators to BPA",
  "change": "Replace the hourly calls to Frontier and GCPUD and to BPA with an automatic meter-data feed to BPA and exception alerts to the RT desk.",
  "reason": "The mail already says these generators are to be metered automatically, by BPA, from mid-August 2001, and that the hourly calls stop then; so the proposal adds nothing, it treats a short episode as 730 hours a month for good, and its 3-minute figure is a split of a ceiling, not an estimate.",
  "research": "Look for mail after August 2001 showing the hourly calls to BPA still being made for Frontier or another generator after automatic metering was due, and for what the call actually took each hour; without that the idea is not new and not ongoing."
}

{
  "name": "Forwarding mail sent to the wrong Bill Williams",
  "change": "Add each person's group to the two \"Bill Williams\" address book names so senders can see which one they are picking.",
  "reason": "The same work and the same fix are already saved as item 13 in decisions.md, 'Forwarding mail sent to the wrong Bill Williams' ($15.30 a month), which cites most of the same williams-w3 sent_items messages.",
  "research": null
}

{
  "name": "Daily hand-forwarding of market reports to Portland traders",
  "change": "Deliver the daily Energy Market Report and the Gas Daily/Power Daily PDFs straight to Portland distribution lists, ending the assistants' daily hand-forwarding.",
  "reason": "The same work and change are already saved as item 10 in decisions.md, 'Hand-forwarding daily market reports to the Portland floor' ($39.95 a month), citing the same williams-w3 messages; the draft's 8 minutes every business day for Gas Daily/Power Daily is also unsupported, since Bill Williams's dense 1/28-2/6 inbox holds all 7 Energy Market Report forwards but only one Gas Daily/Power Daily send (1/31) and one 'not loaded yet' note (2/4).",
  "research": null
}

{
  "name": "Monthly accounting arrangement for meter 98-7266 (TGLO storage fuel at Bammel)",
  "change": "Replace the hand-built monthly accounting arrangement for meter 7266 with a standing evergreen deal pair on contracts 012-41500-05-002 and 012-88494-05-001.",
  "reason": "The mail shows only two moments 20 months apart, does not show the monthly hand-build still happening in 2001 (Farmer was asked for a deal in Feb 2000), and by May 2001 the contracts were 'canceled or expired', so the October 2001 entry looks like cleanup after the storage flow ended, not ongoing monthly work.",
  "research": "Look for mail after February 2000 showing whether Farmer set up the requested deal for 7266, and for any 7266 or TGLO Bammel storage volumes in months after May 2001; if neither exists, the work has ended and the idea fails."
}

{
  "name": "Monthly industrial buyback/deficiency lists",
  "change": "Replace Kenneth Seaman's buyback list, Julie Meyers' spreadsheet and the hand-rebuilt Industrial report with one monthly report from Sitara deal tickets.",
  "reason": "The proposal counts the same list twice: Seaman's buyback list and the Industrial report are one stream of work, which Lloyd took over in February 2000. It counts 45 minutes a month for a report that 1253.eml says nobody had seen 'in a few months'. And it assumes a Sitara report could replace Meyers' spreadsheet, whose contents the mail never shows. Two earlier critics rejected this idea for these same reasons (decisions.md items 90 and 91), and this version answers none of them.",
  "research": "Find what Meyers' 'UPDATED SPREADSHEET' attachments contain, and whether any of it is not already in Sitara buyback tickets (e.g. #148381). Find which months Lloyd actually produced the Industrial report after March 2000. Then estimate only the hand work a ticket report would really remove, likely 30-60 minutes a month."
}

{
  "name": "Real-time congestion revenue notices to Volume Management",
  "change": "A nightly comparison of CAISO congestion awards in CAPS finals against the inc sheet and the ISO flash, emailing only the differences, replaces the hand-totalled notices.",
  "reason": "The same work and change is already saved as item 19, 'Real Time desk's hand-figured congestion revenue emails to Volume Management', and it cites all of this proposal's messages.",
  "research": null
}
